---
const collectiveUrl = 'https://opencollective.com/tus'
---

<div class="sponsor-tus">
  <h2 id="sponsor">Sponsor tus</h2>

  <p>
    tus is an open protocol for resumable file uploads, with open-source
    clients and servers for the web, mobile and the backend. Video platforms,
    cloud providers, databases and developer tools rely on it to get large
    files across flaky networks without starting over.
  </p>

  <p>
    Keeping it reliable takes steady work: reviewing pull requests, fixing
    bugs, cutting releases, keeping implementations interoperable, and bringing
    resumable uploads to the IETF as an HTTP standard. Funding lets maintainers
    spend dedicated time on that. Contributions and expenses are public on Open
    Collective.
  </p>

  <p>
    If your product depends on tus, please consider sponsoring it, either as a
    company or as an individual.
  </p>

  <a class="sponsor-button" href={collectiveUrl}>
    Sponsor tus on Open Collective
  </a>
</div>

<style>
  .sponsor-tus {
    max-inline-size: 44rem;
    margin: 0 auto;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .sponsor-tus p {
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    text-align: start;
  }

  @media screen and (width >= 768px) {
    .sponsor-tus p {
      text-align: center;
    }
  }

  .sponsor-button {
    display: inline-block;
    margin-block-start: var(--space4);
    padding: var(--space3) var(--space6);
    border-radius: 0.25rem;
    background-color: var(--green3);
    color: white;
    font-weight: 500;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .sponsor-button:hover,
  .sponsor-button:focus-visible {
    background-color: var(--green2);
    color: white;
    text-decoration: none;
  }
</style>
